+- REQ-CAPSTONE-4764: The held-out first-win readiness workflow SHALL measure or checkpoint-resume the Experiment 4605 color-permuted variant harness for the live E3 scored agent, scope the run so a Codex wall-clock cap still emits a usable partial artifact, and write `results/experiment_4764_heldout_first_win_readiness.json`. The workflow SHALL verify `arc_solver_kit.offline_arcade()`, importing `experiment_4605_live_integration_scored_agent`, and the Qwen3.5-9B-MTP GGUF cache before proxy work; if any precondition fails, it SHALL write a terminal `blocked_<resource>` artifact rather than fabricate a rate. It SHALL report held-out first-win rate with CI, the prior best held-out first-win rate from prior readiness artifacts, and the delta versus that prior best. It SHALL declare `inference_substrate=live_llm_inference` only when this invocation actually ran the agent live and therefore uses a 60 second duration floor; if this invocation resumes from a checkpoint or lever-cache and only aggregates upstream rows, it SHALL declare `inference_substrate=aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts` and use the 0.0001 second cache floor. If the measured held-out first-win rate is flat at the 0.04 baseline, it SHALL emit `null_delta_methodology_note` and `positive_control_passed=true` so the flat result is read as a genuine null.
